Perfect! Now let me provide you with a comprehensive analysis of the Apache Druid 0.20.0 vulnerability:

## Apache Druid 0.20.0 JavaScript Security Vulnerability Analysis

I've completed a thorough exploration of the Apache Druid codebase at `/root/druid/`. Here's my comprehensive analysis:

### VULNERABILITY OVERVIEW

The vulnerability allows an attacker to bypass the `druid.javascript.enabled` security setting by sending a JSON payload with an empty key `""` containing a JavaScript filter object with `{"enabled": true}`. This works because Jackson deserialization prioritizes injected values over default configuration when processing @JacksonInject parameters.

---

## 1. JAVASCRIPT CONFIGURATION AND SECURITY CHECK

### JavaScriptConfig Class
**File:** `/root/druid/core/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/js/JavaScriptConfig.java`

```java
@PublicApi
public class JavaScriptConfig
{
  public static final int DEFAULT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = 9;
  private static final JavaScriptConfig ENABLED_INSTANCE = new JavaScriptConfig(true);

  @JsonProperty
  private final boolean enabled;

  @JsonCreator
  public JavaScriptConfig(
      @JsonProperty("enabled") boolean enabled
  )
  {
    this.enabled = enabled;
  }

  public boolean isEnabled()
  {
    return enabled;
  }
  // ... equals, hashCode, toString methods
}
```

**Key Issue:** The `JavaScriptConfig` is a simple POJO with `@JsonProperty("enabled")` for deserialization and is injected via `@JacksonInject` into JavaScript-based components.

### JavaScriptModule (Dependency Injection)
**File:** `/root/druid/server/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/guice/JavaScriptModule.java`

```java
public class JavaScriptModule implements Module
{
  @Override
  public void configure(Binder binder)
  {
    JsonConfigProvider.bind(binder, "druid.javascript", JavaScriptConfig.class);
  }
}
```

The module binds `JavaScriptConfig` based on the `druid.javascript` configuration property.

---

## 2. ALL JAVASCRIPT-BASED COMPONENTS WITH @JacksonInject

### A. FILTERS

#### 1. JavaScriptDimFilter (JSON Filter)
**File:** `/root/druid/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/JavaScriptDimFilter.java`

```java
public class JavaScriptDimFilter extends AbstractOptimizableDimFilter implements DimFilter
{
  private final String dimension;
  private final String function;
  @Nullable
  private final ExtractionFn extractionFn;
  @Nullable
  private final FilterTuning filterTuning;
  private final JavaScriptConfig config;

  @JsonCreator
  public JavaScriptDimFilter(
      @JsonProperty("dimension") String dimension,
      @JsonProperty("function") String function,
      @JsonProperty("extractionFn") @Nullable ExtractionFn extractionFn,
      @JsonProperty("filterTuning") @Nullable FilterTuning filterTuning,
      @JacksonInject JavaScriptConfig config  // <-- INJECTED
  )
  {
    Preconditions.checkArgument(dimension != null, "dimension must not be null");
    Preconditions.checkArgument(function != null, "function must not be null");
    this.dimension = dimension;
    this.function = function;
    this.extractionFn = extractionFn;
    this.filterTuning = filterTuning;
    this.config = config;
  }

  // Security check happens when USING the filter, not during deserialization:
  @EnsuresNonNull("predicateFactory")
  private JavaScriptPredicateFactory getPredicateFactory()
  {
    Preconditions.checkState(config.isEnabled(), "JavaScript is disabled");
    // ... rest of method
  }
}
```

**DimFilter Registration (Type Polymorphism):**
**File:** `/root/druid/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/filter/DimFilter.java`

```java
@JsonTypeInfo(use = JsonTypeInfo.Id.NAME, property = "type")
@JsonSubTypes(value = {
    @JsonSubTypes.Type(name = "and", value = AndDimFilter.class),
    @JsonSubTypes.Type(name = "or", value = OrDimFilter.class),
    // ...
    @JsonSubTypes.Type(name = "javascript", value = JavaScriptDimFilter.class),
    // ...
